1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,980
In 1054, a star exploded so bright it appeared during the day.

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:09,190
For 23 days, human history recorded a second sun in the sky.

3
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:14,270
A massive star six thousand light-years away ran out of fuel and collapsed.

4
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:19,180
Pause the video right now. Can you guess what survived that blast?

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,320
It left behind the Crab Nebula, spinning a city-sized neutron star.

6
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:28,600
This dense stellar corpse spins 30 times every single second.

7
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:32,590
One teaspoon of this dead star weighs as much as Mount Everest.

8
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,730
And it all started when...
